  "body": "> Queue a task to fire a change event named \"change\" with changes at window’s CookieStore on window’s responsible event loop.\r\n\r\nThis should use [queue a global task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-global-task) given _window_, to pass along the document when appropriate. But that's pretty minor (and easy for the reader to infer).\r\n\r\nThe trickier question is what task source to use for the queued task. I'm curious which one Chromium uses? If it's kMiscPlatformAPI, then that's bad and we need to pick a new one.",
